 carried  through on the inside the retro grab  handle in front of the passenger seat  gives the dune that old-style beetle  look the handle won't feature in  standard bugs due to safety issues or  the passenger side airbag the doones  ultra modern central display stands in  stark contrast to the retro feel  the oil gauge clock and boost gauge are  also presented as a matching trio the  center console looks clear and  uncluttered drivers shift gears using  the six-speed dual-clutch gearbox  but there is one thing about the bug  that bugs Lhasa and it has to do with  beetles iconic shape yeah he says when  reversing visibility is not that great  but that's the only real - he's noticed  VW hopes the car will revive the dune  buggy lifestyle so what does lassie  think of it the blood is a lifestyle car  that's nice for the summer too bad it's  not a convertible he says but for a  close top car it's great a real summer  car the model VW does plan to offer an  open top version of the dune but beach  buggy fans will have to be patient both  the convertible and standard versions  won't be ready to hit the sand dunes  until 2016 at the earliest
 

